                <div id="tab11" class="content active">

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30 active" data-rel="tab-a-1">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">How does the programme’s format support family business successors in driving change within their business? </p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg" class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-1">50% of the entire course is focused on fixing problems and challenges within your business. You will work privately with your own family business team, aided by professional facilitators, to identify challenges and goals, creating actionable plans tailored to your family enterprise. 


                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-a-2">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">How does the curriculum address the unique challenges faced by family business owners?
                            </p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg" class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-2">Each term, through the Family Business Lab Capstone Projects, you will tackle one critical area of your business - starting from finance, digital transformation, to acquisition, and 100-year succession plan. The programme also acknowledges the significance.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-a-3">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">How do international and domestic immersions enhance the learning experience of participants? </p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg" class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-3">Other than significantly expanding your network across Europe, China and rural India, these immersions will help you gain alternate perspectives on running and expanding your family business by observing global stalwarts. </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-a-4">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">What will be the batch size of the class?</p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg" class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-4">We intend for this programme to be a small close knit community of 40-60 young family leaders.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-a-5">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">Are the travel costs for all immersions covered in the cost of the programme?
                            </p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg" class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-5">The program fees include travel expenses for the rural trek. However, costs for other immersions, such as the INSEAD program and the Canton Fair in China, are optional and will need to be borne by the students.   

                        </p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="faqquestionWrap mb30" data-rel="tab-a-6">
                        <div class="left">
                            <p class="faqHeading">What role does mentorship play in the overall learning experience of the programme?</p>

                            <img  src="https://images.mastersunion.link/uploads/25062025/v1/MainButton3.svg" class="toggler" alt="Icon">
                        </div>
                        <p class="faqanswer" id="tab-a-6">Learners can expect 1:1 mentorship from experienced family business owners, consultants, and CXOs, who provide firsthand insights drawn from their experiences in balancing family dynamics with business innovation. Additionally, many of our mentors hold CXO positions in multinational corporations, equipping learners with global best practices and strategies that can be directly applied to elevate their family enterprises. This blend of personal and global expertise ensures a comprehensive understanding of both family and business leadership.</p>
                    </div>

                </div>
